From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jorge Trigger <lordchronotrigger@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:34:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gfx: release resource caches before resetting a shell session

Function-local strong caches survived graphics teardown. The shell then restores
raw writable segments without ARC releases, losing their ownership. Expose and
release the resource caches after queue drain, and reset their cached GPU IDs.
The real-Metal regression verifies release and residency across two sessions.
This fixes an ownership defect, not a proven cause of the iPad kernel wait.
Pipeline and library caches remain outside this change.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: Release retained Metal resources before the personal iPad shell resets the game
Issue: seedds/nxnative#2098 (related hang only, causality unproven)
